{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.ExtremalPrincipleDoesNotDetermine","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ExtremalPrincipleDoesNotDetermine","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.equal_costs_are_decided_by_the_constraint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.equal_costs_are_decided_by_the_constraint","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ExtremalPrincipleDoesNotDetermine.lean#L103-L113","doc":"**Non-vacuity.**  The freedom is in the cost, not in the arithmetic: hold the\ncost weights EQUAL and the constraint alone does decide, by `|aᵢ|`.  So the\ntheorem above is about the modelling choice, not about an ill-posed comparison. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.two_costs_two_minimisers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.two_costs_two_minimisers","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ExtremalPrincipleDoesNotDetermine.lean#L93-L101","doc":"**The corpus instance in miniature.**  One constraint `x₁ + 2x₂ = 1`.  The\nuniform cost `w = (1,1)` prefers coordinate 2; the reweighted cost `w = (1,4)`\nprefers coordinate 1.  Same feasible set, same optimum *principle*, different\nanswer — which is Option D's Plancherel-vs-Frobenius split, stripped to two\ncoordinates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.both_orderings_achievable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.both_orderings_achievable","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ExtremalPrincipleDoesNotDetermine.lean#L71-L91","doc":"**The refutation.**  For ANY single constraint, both orderings of any two\ncoordinates are achievable by choosing the cost weights — so the extremum\ncarries no information about which coordinate wins.  The cost does, and the cost\nis a modelling choice rather than a consequence of the constraint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.cost_lt_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.cost_lt_iff","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ExtremalPrincipleDoesNotDetermine.lean#L56-L69","doc":"The comparison between two coordinates depends on the constraint only\nthrough `|aᵢ|`, and on the cost only through `wᵢ` — as the single ratio\n`wᵢ / |aᵢ|`.  The target `b` cancels entirely. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.singleSupportCost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.singleSupportCost","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ExtremalPrincipleDoesNotDetermine.lean#L51-L54","doc":"The cost of the single-support solution at a coordinate with constraint\ncoefficient `a` and cost weight `w`: put all the mass there (`x = b / a`) and\npay `w · |x|`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}